plc/texas/bosque-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids in Bosque County came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years for May to June and for November to December, back to 1951. In 2025 the middle ran 209% of normal in June to July and 56% in September to October. May to June is the wettest pair at 8.00 inches normal, January to February the driest at 4.15. Grid 13929 had its driest year in 1954 at 47% of normal.</p>"}
